WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.027
Two ways to cap the blast radius.

2
00:00:02.307 --> 00:00:05.933
In Studio 1 you gated one write tool behind an approval.

3
00:00:06.213 --> 00:00:14.661
An agent from this studio is a bigger problem: it chooses its own steps, holds several tools, and may run for many turns while you look elsewhere.

4
00:00:14.941 --> 00:00:21.469
You can’t review every decision, so the question becomes how much damage the worst run could do, and how to bound it.

5
00:00:21.749 --> 00:00:30.027
Anthropic’s engineering post “How we contain Claude across products” (May 2026) frames the answer in two parts.

6
00:00:30.307 --> 00:00:34.061
The first is supervision: a human in the loop approves actions.

7
00:00:34.341 --> 00:00:46.672
The second is containment: limit what the agent is able to do, with sandboxes, virtual machines, scoped credentials, and egress controls (rules on which network destinations traffic may reach).

8
00:00:46.952 --> 00:01:04.723
The post also names three sources of risk to design against: a user who directs the agent to do harm (deliberately or carelessly), a model that takes a harmful action nobody asked for, and an external attacker who reaches the agent through tools, files, or network content.

9
00:01:05.003 --> 00:01:07.413
The post’s key distinction is between layers.

10
00:01:07.693 --> 00:01:18.189
Defenses in the model (system prompts, classifiers, training) shape what the agent tends to do; because models are probabilistic, they never reach 100%.

11
00:01:18.469 --> 00:01:27.259
Defenses in the environment set hard boundaries: if a credential never enters the sandbox, it cannot be stolen, whatever caused the attempt.

12
00:01:27.539 --> 00:01:36.200
And the content the agent reads (MCP servers, web results, files) is a third surface you limit by restricting tools and access.

13
00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:38.592
Keep that split in mind for the whole week.

14
00:01:38.872 --> 00:01:42.712
Every control you add, ask: is this a tendency or a boundary?

15
00:01:42.992 --> 00:01:45.339
You want both, and you must know which is which.
